    "q-277846": {
      "dom_id": "step-q277846",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Solve the inequality $\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {4}^{x}>7.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}",
      "worked_solution": "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {4}^{x} & >7 \\\\ {4}^{x} & >14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the logarithm to base $4$ of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{4}⁡({4}^{x}) & >{log}_{4}⁡(14) \\\\ x & >{log}_{4}⁡(14).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
