    "q-87581": {
      "dom_id": "step-q87581",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Solve the inequality $3{e}^{x}-4<0.$",
      "worked_solution": "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{x}-4 & <0 \\\\ 3{e}^{x} & <4 \\\\ {e}^{x} & <\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{x}) & <\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3}) \\\\ x & <\\operatorname{ln}⁡4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
