    "q-87718": {
      "dom_id": "step-q87718",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Solve the inequality $5{e}^{x}+2\\le 4.$",
      "worked_solution": "Isolating the exponential term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{e}^{x}+2 & \\le 4 \\\\ 5{e}^{x} & \\le 2 \\\\ {e}^{x} & \\le \\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{x}) & \\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2}{5}) \\\\ x & \\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
