    "q-87888": {
      "dom_id": "step-q87888",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Solve the inequality ${8}^{2-4x}+11>0.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we isolate the exponential term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{8}^{2-4x}+11 & >0 \\\\ {8}^{2-4x} & >-11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, recall that a positive number raised to any real power is always positive. Since $8>0,$ we have\n\n$$\n{8}^{2-4x}>0\n$$\n\nfor every real value of $x.$\n\nIn particular, every value of ${8}^{2-4x}$ is greater than $-11.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{8}^{2-4x}>-11\n$$\n\nfor all real values of $x.$\n\nHence, the original inequality is satisfied for all real numbers.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
