      "name": "Question 18",
      "problem": "Solve the inequality $-(0.33)^{4x+1}\\le (0.12)^{x-4}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $(0.12)^{x-4}$ is always positive and $-(0.33)^{4x+1}$ is always negative, we always have\n\n$$\n-(0.33)^{4x+1}<(0.12)^{x-4}.\n$$\n\nThis means that the given inequality is satisfied by all real values of $x.$",
