    "q-365326": {
      "dom_id": "step-q365326",
      "name": "Question 20",
      "problem": "Solve the inequality $3{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{x-2}>{3}^{2-3x}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Taking the natural logarithm of both sides and applying the laws of logarithms, we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{x-2} & >{3}^{2-3x} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡[3{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{x-2}] & >\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{2-3x}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡3+\\operatorname{ln}⁡[{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{x-2}] & >\\operatorname{ln}⁡({3}^{2-3x}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡3+(x-2)\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{5}) & >(2-3x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡3+(x-2)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5) & >(2-3x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡3+(x-2)(0-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5) & >(2-3x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡3+(2-x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 & >(2-3x)\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡3+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 & >2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\ 3x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 & >2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 \\\\ x(3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5) & >\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5 \\\\ x & >\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
